# Temporary suppressions for the `security (typescript)` Trivy image scan
# (typescript/typescript.dockerfile), see PR #108, run 40736408950,
# job 122986042922.
#
# All 18 findings below live in vendored/transitive dependencies that ship
# inside packages which are ALREADY at their latest published version as of
# 2026-10-28, so there is no newer release to bump to yet:
#   - undici (3 CVEs): bundled transitively inside npm@12.2.1's own
#     node_modules, pulled in by npm's internal HTTP client deps. Fixed
#     upstream in undici 6.29.1, 7.30.1, 8.12.2, but npm has not vendored a
#     patched undici yet.
#   - Go stdlib / golang.org/x/net / golang.org/x/text (15 CVEs): baked into
#     the native tsc binary, @typescript/typescript-linux-x64@7.0.2
#     (TypeScript 7's Go-compiled native compiler), from the Go toolchain and
#     modules it was built against.
#
# Revisit when this suppression expires: re-run Trivy against the
# typescript kit image. If npm and/or @typescript/typescript-linux-x64 have
# published newer versions that pull in patched undici/Go dependencies,
# bump them and drop the corresponding entries below. If not, extend the
# expiry only after a fresh review of the current advisory state -- do not
# blindly re-up these dates.

